[Variation "Réti Opening: Anglo-Slav Variation"]
[ECO "A13"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "qgd-setup,c5-break"]
[Kind "main"]

1. Nf3 d5 { Takes the centre with a pawn and stops e4. }
2. c4 e6 { Backs up d5, so if White takes Black recaptures with the pawn. It also frees the c8 bishop. }
3. g3 ( 3. d4 Nf6 { This is a Queen's Gambit Declined by transposition. } 4. Nc3 Be7 )
3... Nf6 { Develops a piece and keeps an eye on e4 and d5. }
4. Bg2 Be7 { Clears f8 so Black can castle next. }
5. O-O O-O { The king is safe; now Black can fight for the centre. }
6. b3 ( 6. d4 dxc4 { Black takes the pawn because ...a6 and ...b5 will keep it, or win the time back. } 7. Qc2 a6 { Prepares ...b5 so the extra pawn can be kept. } 8. Qxc4 b5 9. Qc2 Bb7 )
6... c5 { Strikes at the centre as soon as the king is safe, instead of waiting to see what White does. }
7. Bb2 Nc6 { Brings the knight into the centre where it adds to the pressure on d4. }
8. e3 b6 { Prepares ...Bb7 so the bishop faces White's g2 bishop on the long diagonal. Plan: ...Bb7, then ...Rc8 or ...Qe7. If White plays d4, trade on d4 and keep the pieces active. } *
